&lt;/button>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>
&lt;h2>Conversion utilities&lt;span class="hx-absolute -hx-mt-20" id="conversion-utilities">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#conversion-utilities" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h2>&lt;p>Two helper functions support the soot-density-based workflow from the
original FDS+Evac guide:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;code>extinction_from_soot_density(soot_density_mg_per_m3)&lt;/code> &amp;ndash; converts
soot density to extinction using &lt;code>K = K_m * rho_s * 1e-6&lt;/code>, where &lt;code>K_m&lt;/code>
(&lt;code>mass_extinction_coefficient_m2_per_kg&lt;/code>, default 8700 m²/kg) is the FDS
default mass-specific extinction coefficient (see
&lt;a href="https://pedestriandynamics.org/pyFDS-Evac/fundamentals/extinction/">Extinction coefficient&lt;/a>
).&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;code>speed_from_soot_density(base_speed, soot_density_mg_per_m3)&lt;/code> &amp;ndash;
computes the reduced walking speed directly from soot density.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
